# Source: https://github.com/arq5x/bedtools2/issues/980
# Symptom: R-style row-name prefix in first column shifts all field indices;
#   bedtools sort throws "terminate called after throwing an instance of
#   'std::invalid_argument'  what():  stoll" because the chromosome field is
#   parsed as the literal row label and the coordinate fields receive strings.
# The pattern arises when data is exported from an R data.frame with
# row.names=TRUE (default) and write.table() without col.names=FALSE.
             chr       pos   pos_end strand
 cg18478105 chr20  63216297  63216299      +
 cg09835024  chrX  24054522  24054524      +
 cg14361672  chr9 128701656 128701658      -
